@@ -18,6 +18,14 @@ Sources are configured with the `SOURCES` env var, a JSON object:
 { "github": { "secret": "dev-secret", "target": "http://localhost:4000/in" } }
 ```
 
+A source can slow down its retries with an optional `retry` object. The delay starts at `baseDelayMs` (default 100), doubles on each retry and is capped at `maxDelayMs` (default: no cap). Invalid values stop startup.
+
+```json
+{ "acme": { "secret": "...", "target": "https://acme.example/in", "retry": { "baseDelayMs": 60000, "maxDelayMs": 600000 } } }
+```
+
+Delays are looked up by source when each retry is scheduled, so a config change affects retries already in the queue from their next attempt on.
+
 ```sh
 npm install
 npm test                                 # uses an in-memory queue; no Postgres needed
